    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d521">

                <pb facs="0578" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg566"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Bolivia/152: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-04-30T11:00:00-04:00">April 30, 1942—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:28 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>280. Department’s 238, April 27, 8 p.m. Argentines have already bought at least
                    175 tons of rubber. Shipments are now being made by air to Cochabamba taking
                    advantage of low LAB<anchor n="5" xml:id="d521-f1"/> freight rate and thence by
                    rail to Buenos Aires. Price of recent market reported reliably to have been 56
                    cents per pound c.i.f. Buenos Aires which works out about 48 cents f.o.b.
                    Beni.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d521-f1" n="5" xml:id="d521-f1-content">
                <p>Lloyd Aéreo Boliviano.</p>
